{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ZEP",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to her that is filthy and polluted, to the oppressing city!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She obeyed not the voice; she received not correction; she trusted not in the LORD; she drew not near to her God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Her princes within her ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " roaring lions; her judges ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " evening wolves; they gnaw not the bones till the morrow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Her prophets are light ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " treacherous persons: her priests have polluted the sanctuary, they have done violence to the law.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The just LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the midst of her; he will not do iniquity: every morning doth he bring his judgment to light, he faileth not; but the unjust knoweth no shame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have cut off the nations: their towers are desolate; I made their streets waste, that none passeth by: their cities are destroyed, so that there is no man, that there is no inhabitant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said, Surely thou wilt fear me, thou wilt receive instruction; so their dwelling should not be cut off, however I punished them: but they rose early, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " corrupted all their doings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore wait ye upon me, saith the LORD, until the day that I rise up to the prey: for my determination ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to gather the nations, that I may assemble the kingdoms, to pour upon them my indignation, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all my fierce anger: for all the earth shall be devoured with the fire of my jealousy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For then will I turn to the people a pure language, that they may all call upon the name of the LORD, to serve him with one consent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From beyond the rivers of Cush my suppliants, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the daughter of my dispersed, shall bring my offering.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In that day shalt thou not be ashamed for all thy doings, in which thou hast transgressed against me: for then I will take away out of the midst of thee them that rejoice in thy pride, and thou shalt no more be haughty because of my holy mountain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will also leave in the midst of thee an afflicted and poor people, and they shall trust in the name of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The remnant of Israel shall not do iniquity, nor speak lies; neither shall a deceitful tongue be found in their mouth: for they shall feed and lie down, and none shall make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " afraid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sing, O daughter of Zion; shout, O Israel; be glad and rejoice with all the heart, O daughter of Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD hath taken away thy judgments, he hath cast out thy enemy: the King of Israel, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the midst of thee: thou shalt not see evil any more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In that day it shall be said to Jerusalem, Fear thou not: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Zion, Let not thy hands be slack.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD thy God in the midst of thee ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mighty; he will save, he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love, he will joy over thee with singing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will gather ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sorrowful for the solemn assembly, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are of thee, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to whom",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the reproach of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a burden.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, at that time I will undo all that afflict thee: and I will save her that halteth, and gather her that was driven out; and I will get them praise and fame in every land where they have been put to shame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZEP.3.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ZEP.3.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At that time will I bring you ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "again",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", even in the time that I gather you: for I will make you a name and a praise among all people of the earth, when I turn back your captivity before your eyes, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
